{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"meagre-grassgreen-waterdogs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nMake `src/rebar/_store/push.py` the authoritative CAS retry implementation before any workflow migrates. The current core stops after three merge attempts and discards the clean merge produced on its final iteration; the workflow carries five retries plus a final push. The core is also intentionally best-effort, while the reconciler's ephemeral commit-back requires an opt-in fail-loud disposition.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Extend `push_tickets_branch(base_path, *, strict=False)`; preserve the default for every existing caller.\n- Use five merge/retry cycles and perform the final push after the fifth successful merge.\n- Centralize strict failure reporting: print a distinct reason plus `N unpushed commits on <remote>/<branch>..HEAD` to stderr, then exit nonzero.\n- Cover terminal declines, rebase/merge-recovery guard, both store-epoch guards, final-push exhaustion, lock timeout, `sync.push=off`, `sync.push=async`, malformed destination config, and a missing configured remote.\n- Preserve warning-and-return behavior byte-for-byte for the paired best-effort paths.\n- Emit no ticket event and do not resurrect `BRIDGE_ALERT`.\n- Keep `push_tickets_branch` push-only; dirty-tree staging/commit belongs to the dependent child.\n- Update concurrency documentation to distinguish default best effort from opt-in strict delivery.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse real temporary git repositories for convergence and rejection, in-process fault injection at the actual guard/lock seams for the strict/best-effort branch matrix, and the existing real epoch fixtures for both epoch sites.\n\nRED-first oracle:\n- a deterministic competitor wins five pushes; current core exhausts three attempts and the expected remote/local convergence is RED;\n- strict policy rejection must exit nonzero with the exact git reason, escalating unpushed count, and no new event file; current code returns;\n- every strict branch has a paired best-effort control;\n- large rejection stderr is classified by the Python core rather than YAML extraction;\n- mutation removes the final push and makes the contention oracle RED; warn-and-return mutation makes the strict matrix RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Five retry merges plus the final push converge after five deterministic competing pushes.\n- [ ] Every strict failure branch exits nonzero with its distinct reason and unpushed count on stderr.\n- [ ] Strict `off`, `async`, malformed destination, and missing remote configurations fail explicitly.\n- [ ] Every paired best-effort case returns normally and preserves local commits and working-tree state.\n- [ ] Strict failure writes no ticket event and never emits `BRIDGE_ALERT`.\n- [ ] Direct `push_tickets_branch` remains push-only.\n- [ ] Existing narrow-refspec, stash/pop, epoch-guard, and rejection-classification contracts remain green.\n- [ ] Focused pytest nodes, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` pass.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\n`strict` is keyword-only and defaults false, so existing CLI, MCP, library, importer, and store-write callers retain their contract. No persisted schema changes. This prerequisite lands unused and can be reverted safely before the dependent workflow cutover.","id":"953a-d616-52d3-4efe","parent_id":"1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770","priority":1,"tags":["bridge","store","reliability"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add strict CAS push semantics and complete the retry budget"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786142401705629001,"uuid":"af0f8c7b-350d-4514-a59a-1ae989f87029"}